# Source art. The originals stay on the machine that drew them; the web copies
# under public/ are what the site serves and what belongs in the repo. Each
# pattern has an encoder in scripts/ that turns one into the other.
# NB: gitignore has no trailing comments — a `#` after a pattern becomes part
# of the pattern, which silently stops it matching anything.
#   habitat-*.png   -> public/habitats/  via encode-habitat.ps1
habitat-*.png
#   *-concept.png   -> public/concepts/  via encode-concept.ps1
*-concept.png
#   room art        -> public/rooms/     via encode-room.ps1
# Globs, not a list of filenames. A list has to be edited every time a room is
# painted, and if it is not, the next `git add -A` commits the source — which
# is exactly how 15 MB of PNGs reached the repo twice. These three cover every
# room name the project uses and any that follow the same habit.
*-room.png
*-hall.png
*-bench.png

# Sprites are fetched at build time, not committed (scripts/fetch-sprites.mjs)
public/sprites/
